  "title": "Breaking Changes & New Serving Profiles API",
  "summary": "Vertex AI introduces a new Serving Profiles API for managing model serving configurations, alongside several breaking changes. Developers must update their code to handle newly required parameters, altered field types, and read-only properties.",
  "details": "This update brings significant changes to the Vertex AI API. Most notably, a new `ServingProfiles` resource has been added, complete with `create`, `get`, `list`, `delete`, and `patch` methods, enabling more granular control over model serving configurations. \n\n**Breaking Changes:**\n1.  **Required Parameters:** The `parent` and `name` parameters are now strictly required in various contexts. For the new `servingProfiles` methods, these are explicitly marked as required. This aligns with previous announcements regarding `name` parameters becoming mandatory.\n2.  **Type Change:** The `structuredPrompt` property within `CloudAiLargeModelsVisionExperimentsResponseProEditResult` and `CloudAiLargeModelsVisionGenerateVideoExperimentsProEditConfig` has changed its type from `object` to `string`. This will break existing integrations expecting an object.\n3.  **Read-Only Fields:** Several properties are now read-only/immutable: `nextPageToken` and `servingProfiles` in `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ListServingProfilesResponse`, `createTime` and `updateTime` in `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ServingProfile`, and `gcsMetricsUri` in `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1TuningJob`. Attempts to set these values will now fail.\n\nAdditionally, the `projects.updateCacheConfig` method now supports an `updateMask` parameter for partial updates to cache configurations. For `agents` methods, the `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/aiplatform` OAuth scope is now the primary authorization scope, with `cloud-platform` moving to a secondary position, reinforcing the shift towards more specific permissions.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
  "interesting_score": 9,
  "tags": [
    "Breaking Change",
    "New API",
    "AI/ML",
    "Vertex AI",
    "Serving Profiles"
  ],
